> A small geometric comparison

The native six-city fixture supplies planar points, and the existing native
Euclidean-distance helper builds its complete matrix. The greedy call and
bounded permutation enumerator return their own actual tours. The reference
enumerates every anchored tour for six cities, retaining the first strict
minimum of the same sequential rounded cost objective. This small exhaustive
comparator is intentionally expensive and is not a scalable replacement for the
greedy scan.

Both panels use equal geometric scales and the same city coordinates. Every
plotted segment follows a returned route. Floating Euclidean distances and cost
sums remain rounded; arbitrary noninteger weights are not turned into an
exact-real optimality certificate by enumeration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nearest_tsp_geometry.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto points = dm::algorithms::nearest_neighbor_tsp_demo_points();
    auto d = dm::algorithms::euclidean_tsp_distances(points);
    auto greedy = dm::algorithms::nearest_neighbor_tsp(d);
    auto optimal = dm::algorithms::enumerate_tsp(d);
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
    std::vector<double> px, py;
    for (auto[x, y] : points) {
        px.push_back(x);
        py.push_back(y);
    }
    std::print("| native method | actual route | rounded cost |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n| nearest neighbor | " "{} | {} |\n| bounded enumeration | {} | {} |\n",
               greedy.tour, greedy.cost, optimal.tour, optimal.cost);
    for (auto &entry : std::vector<std::pair<std::string, dm::algorithms::TourResult>>{{"nearest neighbor", greedy}, {"bounded enumeration", optimal}}) {
        std::vector<double> x, y;
        for (auto id : entry.second.tour) {
            x.push_back(points[id].first);
            y.push_back(points[id].second);
        }
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.line(x, y, "actual route", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(
            px, py, "city coordinates", {17, 24, 39}, 6).size(850, 850).margins(
            95, 35, 60, 70).x_limits(-1, 5).y_limits(-1, 5).title(entry.first).x_label("x").y_label("y");
        layout.add(p);
    }
    layout.size(1700, 850).fit_panels().save_svg("build/nearest_tsp_geometry.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| native method | actual route | rounded cost |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| nearest neighbor | [0, 4, 3, 5, 2, 1, 0] | 15.22677276241436 |
| bounded enumeration | [0, 3, 5, 2, 1, 4, 0] | 15.15298244508295 |
